1
00:00:00,070 --> 00:00:01,315
Could every planet fit

2
00:00:01,315 --> 00:00:03,525
between you and the Moon?

3
00:00:03,680 --> 00:00:04,090
Yep!

4
00:00:04,090 --> 00:00:05,868
All seven FIT...

5
00:00:05,868 --> 00:00:07,170
side by side.

6
00:00:07,170 --> 00:00:08,167
Barely.

7
00:00:08,220 --> 00:00:09,195
Jupiter and Saturn

8
00:00:09,195 --> 00:00:11,000
hog two-thirds of the gap...

9
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:12,350
and Saturn has to take

10
00:00:12,350 --> 00:00:14,300
its rings OFF.

11
00:00:14,400 --> 00:00:15,453
One catch...

12
00:00:15,453 --> 00:00:17,592
the Moon has to be FAR.

13
00:00:17,592 --> 00:00:19,060
It drifts in and out

14
00:00:19,060 --> 00:00:20,008
every month...

15
00:00:20,008 --> 00:00:22,767
by up to a whole NEPTUNE.

16
00:00:22,800 --> 00:00:24,428
So on a close night...

17
00:00:24,428 --> 00:00:26,394
Neptune sleeps outside.

